## 🚀 Getting Started

### **1. Clone the repo**
```bash
git clone https://github.com/<yourname>/poke-center.git
cd poke-center

2. Run locally
Use any static server:
npx serve
Or open index.html directly in a browser.

3. Deploy to GitHub Pages
Push to GitHub and enable Pages in repo settings.

🧩 Adding a New Collection
1. Create a folder:
/collections/<NewCollectionId>/

2. Add cardData.js with an array of card objects:
export default [
  {
    cardNumber: 1,
    name: "Example Pokémon",
    rarity: "Rare",
    file: "001.png"
  },
  ...
];

3. Add logo to:
/assets/logos/

4. Add entry to manifest.js:
{ id: "<NewCollectionId>", name: "New Set Name", logo: "<logoFile>" }
Done — the app will automatically detect and load it.

